{"tool_name":"liputils","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"liputils","home":"https://github.com/Stemanz/liputils/","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"A Python module to manage individual fatty acid moieties from complex lipids.\n\nA small Python package to manipulate complex lipids.","addition_date":"2021-01-18T10:25:43Z","last_update_date":"2021-02-17T07:01:05Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Library"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:liputils","credit":[{"email":"giulia.chiesa@unimi.it","name":"Giulia Chiesa","typeEntity":"Person"},{"email":"stefano.manzini@unimi.it","name":"Stefano Manzini","typeEntity":"Person"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Data retrieval","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2422"},{"term":"Essential dynamics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3891"},{"term":"Parsing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_1812"}]}],"name":"liputils","owner":"Niclaskn","publication":[{"doi":"10.1038/S41598-020-70259-9","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2020, The Author(s).Lipidomic analyses address the problem of characterizing the lipid components of given cells, tissues and organisms by means of chromatographic separations coupled to high-resolution, tandem mass spectrometry analyses. A number of software tools have been developed to help in the daunting task of mass spectrometry signal processing and cleaning, peak analysis and compound identification, and a typical finished lipidomic dataset contains hundreds to thousands of individual molecular lipid species. To provide researchers without a specific technical expertise in mass spectrometry the possibility of broadening the exploration of lipidomic datasets, we have developed liputils, a Python module that specializes in the extraction of fatty acid moieties from individual molecular lipids. There is no prerequisite data format, as liputils extracts residues from RefMet-compliant textual identifiers and from annotations of other commercially available services. We provide three examples of real-world data processing with liputils, as well as a detailed protocol on how to readily process an existing dataset that can be followed with basic informatics skills.","authors":[{"name":"Busnelli M."},{"name":"Chiesa G."},{"name":"Colombo A."},{"name":"Kiamehr M."},{"name":"Manzini S."}],"date":"2020-12-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Scientific Reports","title":"liputils: a Python module to manage individual fatty acid moieties from complex lipids"},"pmcid":"PMC7415148","pmid":"32770020"}],"topic":[{"term":"Endocrinology and metabolism","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3407"},{"term":"Informatics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0605"},{"term":"Lipids","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0153"},{"term":"Metabolomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3172"},{"term":"Proteomics experiment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3520"}]},"bioschemas":{"name":"liputils","home":"https://bio.tools/liputils","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"A Python module to manage individual fatty acid moieties from complex lipids.\n\nA small Python package to manipulate complex lipids.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:liputils/cmd/github.com","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"binaries":{"freeness":null,"registration":null},"packages":null,"source_packages":false,"sourcecode":{"free":null,"interpreted":true,"license":null,"public":true,"readme":false,"repository":{"anonymous":null,"online":null}}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"license":{"open_source":true,"osi":true},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":4,"citations":[{"count":1,"year":"2021"},{"count":1,"year":"2022"},{"count":1,"year":"2024"},{"count":1,"year":"2026"}],"doi":"10.1038/s41598-020-70259-9","pmcid":"PMC7415148","pmid":"32770020","ref_count":3,"refs":